:name: STM32F4 Discovery
:description: Boots the flight controller firmware on a simulated STM32F4DISCOVERY.

# Run from the repo root. Pass another ELF with `$bin = @path` before including.
$bin ?= @firmware/target/thumbv7em-none-eabihf/release/firmware

using sysbus
mach create "blackbox"

# Renode's own description of the board: the STM32F407VG and the parts around
# it, including the green LED on PD12.
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/stm32f4_discovery-kit.repl

# Renode clocks the timers at a fixed 10 MHz and doesn't model the clock tree.
# The firmware runs from the 16 MHz internal oscillator with no bus
# prescalers, so TIM2 (embassy-time) and TIM3 (the control loop) count at
# 16 MHz. Change these with the firmware's clocks.
timer2 Frequency 16000000
timer3 Frequency 16000000

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
"""
runMacro $reset

# `runMacro $timing` prints how well the control loop keeps its deadline. The
# counters are LOOP_TIMING's fields in order, and TIM3's ARR + 1 is the counts
# in one period.
macro timing
"""
    python "bus = monitor.Machine.SystemBus; a = bus.GetSymbolAddress('LOOP_TIMING'); r = lambda o: bus.ReadDoubleWord(a + o); counts = bus.ReadDoubleWord(0x4000042C) + 1; print('ticks %d, overruns %d, max jitter %d ns' % (r(0), r(4), r(8) * 1000000 // counts))"
"""

# Log each time the green LED changes state.
logLevel -1 gpioPortD.UserLED

start
